# - Qobuz, Aknose artist page, Music Story biography and discography (opened 2026-10-20): originally from Guadeloupe, urban music artist fusing traditional West Indian sounds with contemporary influences, style notably inspired by bouyon; Coco Mwen Ka Monté Mon'n on 9 January 2024; Kak Up on 9 February 2024, a collaboration with Gwada G; Minimum video on 28 March 2024, directed by Griffit Vision, composed by Ray da Prince; Palabras on 31 January 2025 with YSN; Lè an pa siw ou si mwen with Larose. Discography listings opened on the same page: 0690 (12 December 2023, released by aknose), Ho nana (Loxymore One Shot) (20 October 2023, LOXYMORE), KAK UP (9 February 2024, Vadore Concept Groupe), MINIMUM (15 March 2024, M B I Family), Kalollipop (14 June 2024, M B I Family), Manawa (6 September 2024, Hakuna Music Company), Palabras (31 January 2025, Hakuna Music Company and MBI Family), What I do (7 March 2025, MBI FAMILY), Pooch (Radio Edit) (4 April 2025, Mjtx), Coulie Coulie (28 June 2025, MBI FAMILY), Close your mouth (7 November 2025), Conakry (26 November 2025), Bonne humeur (9 December 2025).
# - quel-dj.com, Playlist Shatta and Bouyon (opened 2026-10-20 via search): Moustik, a collaboration between producer 1T1 and Aknose, released 29 September 2023, modern bouyon wave with Guadeloupean Creole lyrics, the dancer compared to a mosquito on the dancefloor.
# - Qobuz, 1T1 artist page and discography (opened 2026-10-20 via search, and wave 2 dossier on disk): Moustik dated 28 September 2023; Bidiba Bidibou with Aknose and Softee on 2 June 2023; Bad Girls with Aknose and Nils on 1 December 2023; Mas La Rivé on 12 January 2024 credited to 1T1 featuring Theomaa, Aknose, DJ Softee, Dj TKrys, Bismok, Jicypie, Dj Kylled and Lejuh; the 1T1 Music Story biography lists "Aknose - Moustik" among the tracks that made his name.
# - AB BOYZ Music, label article on 1T1, 6 May 2024 (opened 2026-10-20 via search): 1T1 keeps producing hit records such as Moustik with Aknose and Sicré Kon Miel.
# - Shazam (search results, 2026-10-20): New Bouyon Wave #1 by D0 Production featuring Tiitii NBA, Nils, Dj Softee, Aknose and Theomaa, released 29 September 2023 on 2873529 Records DK, 160 BPM; Gwo Kok Pou Gwo Kokote by Gomko featuring Aknose, released 21 June 2023 on 2886154 Records DK, in French, 155 BPM, songwriter Gael Aknose Rampath; KKM by DJ LUCHSHIY featuring AKNOSE, released 24 April 2023 on LUCHSHIY AND BRO, 160 BPM, songwriters Corane Vincent and Gael Rampath; Ding Dong by Dj Tkrys and Aknose, released 28 September 2018 on Le Bon Tuyau Music; La Manigance, a 2025 collective single featuring Aknose among TKS 2G, Mikado, P.L.L, Junior, N'Ken, Le Jèm'ss, Lijay, YSN, Da Nillo and Vanou.
# - Deezer, Bouyon bass playlist listing (search result, 2026-10-20): "Aknose - Moustik" by 1T1, duration 2:27, writer Gael Rampath, composer Terry Baptiste.
# - Boomplay (search result, 2026-10-20): Qualité Quantité by LSB featuring Aknose, released in 2023, duration 2:35.
# - CCN, Caraib Creole News, interview with Maïté Berchel-Bordin, published 13 December 2025 (opened 2026-10-20): in Guadeloupe the most emblematic bouyon artists of the moment are Lejuh, 1T1, Theomaa, Piscine OSP, Aknose and Shanika.
# Note: no verified official social URL for Aknose was confirmed during this research, so sameAs is empty. The songwriter name Gael Rampath is reported exactly as platform credits publish it, with its sources named each time.

